            "review_id": "REV_12614342_p1_10",
            "reviewer_id": "User_p1_10",
            "review_title": "Review at Burger King",
            "review_text": "Mike\nAirlie Beach, Australia6 contributions\n1\nSlow food take-away.\nMar 2020\nOn the 21st of March my partner and I decided to grab a quick bite before we had to board our flight. The two ladies that served us were nice, spoke great English and had a professional customer service approach. We ordered 2 meals.. then there was an announcement over the speaker that our flight was boarding before scheduled. We kindly asked the guy in the back roughly how long it would take we have to board soon, he ignored us. Five mins later we were getting a little bit more impatient and asked again, he smirked and started packing the chips in the bag slowly, literally one by one.. knowing that we were in a hurry. The two ladies were wearing gloves and face masks, because the Covid-19 was getting around.. yet the guy in the back wasn't wearing a mask/gloves. The burgers were ready and the guy in the back was still patiently adding the chips to the bag one by one. We were so frustrated that we grabbed the burgers and went to board our flight, as we walked away he starts laughing. I was extremely disgusted by the attitude of this worker and felt that I needed to write a review about it. Management really need to review this employee and perhaps do a work performance review, no doubt.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten April 1, 2020",
